original_sparse_ownership.json, original_sparse_ownership.py and corresponding
sparse-noise cases in rust_snapshot_contracts.rs are adapted from itpyi/magna,
revision 56847478c840395735146ef1e1ccdc3d8aedc10f:
tests/core/test_runtime_ownership.py::RuntimeOwnershipTests.test_sparse_noise_equals_dense_categories_and_isolation.

Original repository: https://github.com/itpyi/magna
Full license: original_many_record_input.LICENSE in this directory.

The complete unchanged original method validates100 dense and200 sparse draws,
including caller table mutation and malformed action checks. The fixture retains
all100 original seeds, categorical choices, named actions and raw/canonical exact
likelihood ratios. Rust maps foreign channel order by explicit action identity,
replays all100 choices and compares its own sparse/dense100-seed streams; it does
not claim default Python RNG sequence or private native index equality. Generator,
source, frontend and identified prebuilt helper hashes bind the observations.
